  "source": "---\ntitle: Parts\nconcept: parts\ndescription: One word, griddle, in every place a part can hold it.\nnamespaces:\n  - example.org/cooking/kitchen\n---\n\nA paragraph with a griddle (line 9).\n\n:::tabs\n### The griddle tab\n\nTab body with a griddle (line 15).\n\n### Second tab\n\nNo bad word here.\n:::\n\n:::accordion\n### Accordion griddle title\n\nAccordion body with a griddle (line 25).\n:::\n\n:::human\nA human-only segment with a griddle (line 29).\n:::\n\n:::llm\nAn LLM text with a griddle (line 33).\n:::\n\n```terminal title=\"Terminal griddle title\" id=griddle\n@step Terminal step griddle\n$ echo griddle\ngriddle\n```\n\n```filetree\n@step Tree step griddle\nsrc/\n  griddle.go  # a note with a griddle\n```\n\n```chart\nkind: bar\ntitle: Chart griddle title\nx: { label: dish, values: [griddle, wok] }\ny: { label: count }\nseries:\n  - name: Series griddle name\n    data: [3, 4]\n```\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  griddle1[\"Mermaid griddle label\"] --> wok1[\"Wok\"]\n```\n\n```animation\npill a \"Animation griddle label\"\npill b \"Wok\"\na -> b \"link\"\n@step Animation griddle caption\nsend \"go\" a -> b\n@step Second caption, no bad word\nnote b: a note with a griddle\n```\n\n```tierlist title=\"Tier griddle title\"\nS: Wok\nA: Tier griddle item\n```\n\n```alignment title=\"Which pan?\"\nx: low effort .. high effort\ny: high impact .. low impact\nlow effort / high impact \"Cell griddle label\": Wok\n```\n",
